  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 34,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.088,
            0.689,
            0.108
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Also it is divisible by 6 if it is divisible by 2 and 3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.108,
            0.833,
            0.129
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If the 6-digit number is divisible by 15 then it ends with 0 and 5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.133,
            0.574,
            0.154
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose the 6-digit number is abcdef."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.154,
            0.577,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since it is divisible by 15, so, f = 0 or 5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.173,
            0.642,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If f = 0, then original number will be abcde0."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.194,
            0.846,
            0.232
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "After reversing the digits it becomes 0edcba which is not a six digit number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.233,
            0.309,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, f = 5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.253,
            0.833,
            0.292
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Also, the new number after reversing the digits is divisible by 2. So, a = 2, 4, 6, 8, (a ≠ 0)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.293,
            0.501,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, possible numbers are —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.313,
            0.708,
            0.333
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For a = 2, f = 5, and sum of th digits is divisible by 3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.333,
            0.553,
            0.353
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "200025, 200055, 200085, 202005, … ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.358,
            0.46,
            0.378
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Find more such numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.388,
            0.847,
            0.464
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. Deepak claims, “There are some multiples of 11 which, when doubled, are still multiples of 11. But other multiples of 11 don’t remain multiples of 11 when doubled”. Examine if his conjecture is true; explain your conclusion."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.469,
            0.484,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Deepak’s conjecture is false."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.49,
            0.543,
            0.509
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let n be a multiple of 11 so n = 11k"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.509,
            0.638,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When doubled the result 2n = 22k = 11 × (2k)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.539,
            0.847,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12. Determine whether the statements below are ‘Always True’, ‘Sometimes True’, or ‘Never True’. Explain your reasoning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.581,
            0.847,
            0.62
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) The product of a multiple of 6 and a multiple of 3 is a multiple of 9."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.623,
            0.847,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) The sum of three consecutive even numbers will be divisible by 6."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.666,
            0.846,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) If abcdef is a multiple of 6, then badcef will be a multiple of 6."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.689,
            0.649,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) 8 (7b – 3) – 4 (11b + 1) is a multiple of 12."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.718,
            0.204,
            0.735
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.736,
            0.385,
            0.756
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Always true."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.759,
            0.389,
            0.779
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Always true."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.783,
            0.385,
            0.804
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Always true."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.807,
            0.374,
            0.827
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) Never true."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.837,
            0.847,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13. Choose any 3 numbers. When is their sum divisible by 3? Explore all possible cases and generalise."
            }
          ]
        },
